  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of people reached through Information, Education and Communication on DRR
2. % of population benefitted through Hazard and risk assessment mapping and impact modelling
3. % increase of population and authorities with enhanced understanding of earthquake and urban risks
4. Number of people covered by early action/contingency plans
5. Number of municipal and provincial EOCs operational with minimal functional benchmark
6. Number of Provincial Earthquake Response Framework (PERF) formulated based on the earthquake risk scenario and anticipated
7. Inter-provincial and inter-municipal coordination mechanism established and formalized
8. Number of cluster members trained to integrate protection issues in the cluster contingency plans
9. Number of provincial level key clusters specific contingency plans prepared for effective response
10. Number of community small-scale infrastructures and facilities built or protected
11. Number of community volunteers, as CERT members, trained and equipped on life saving response skills and readiness
12. Community readiness attested and ensured through conduct of number of emergency simulation exercises
13. Number of security forces trained on technological solutions
14. Number of demonstration houses retrofitted to illustrate technical solution for replication

15. Number of Shared Learning Dialogues with provincial, local level and private sectors</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">NA</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 20,559 population reached through information, education and communication on DRR
- % population benefitted through hazard and risk assessment mapping and impact modelling
- 1 Provincial Earthquake Response Framework (PERF) prepared for earthquake risk scenario
- 1 inter-provincial and inter-municipal coordination mechanism established
- 2 Provincial level cluster specific contingency plans prepared
- 1000 CERT members trained and mobilized
- 8 emergency simulation exercises conducted
- 30 security forces trained on technological solutions
- 3 shared learning dialogues organized</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">- 2 Sensitization and Dissemination workshops at Lumbini province and 1 municipalities completed.
- Baseline KAP survey completed and final report prepared
- Rapid vulnerability assessment of 4000 Hhs completed:
- 1 Provincial Earthquake Response framework based on the shared understanding of earthquake risk scenario and anticipated impacts prepared.
- Inter/Intra-provincial simulation exercises (table top), 3 at provincial level and 4 at municipal level completed.
- 30 CERT members trained
- 1 LEOC strengthened</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
